    "title": "<p>Diagnostic criteria and differential diagnosis of lymphomatoid papulosis {29719017}</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "Kempf W",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 708.45pt; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"945\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 90.15pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"120\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Histological subtype</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 94.15pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"126\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Phenotype</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.55pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"266\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Diagnostic histopathological and genetic criteria</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 140.3pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"187\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Differential diagnosis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Discriminating features</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 90.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"120\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">A</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">(80%)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 94.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"126\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">CD4+, CD8&minus;, CD30+</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"266\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Wedge-shaped infiltrate with scattered or small clusters of large pleomorphic CD30+ cells (sometimes multinucleated or immunoblastic/Reed&ndash;Sternberg&ndash;like) and numerous inflammatory cells, i.e. small lymphocytes, neutrophils, and/or eosinophils</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{7104214; 10845893; 15096372}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 140.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"187\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Mycosis fungoides, tumour stage</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Clinical evolution with preceding patches and plaques</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 140.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"187\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Hodgkin lymphoma (almost always secondary cutaneous involvement)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Staging: nodal involvement</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 140.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"187\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Primary cutaneous anaplastic large cell lymphoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Clinical presentation: rapidly growing large tumour or multifocal nodules; cohesive sheets of large CD30+ T&nbsp;cells</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 90.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"120\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">B</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">(&lt;&nbsp;5%)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 94.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"126\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">CD4+, CD8&minus;, CD30+/&minus;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.55pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"266\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Epidermotropic infiltrate of small atypical CD30+ or CD30&minus; cells with cerebriform nuclei</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">{7104214; 10845893; 15096372}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 140.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"187\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Mycosis fungoides, patch/plaque stage</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Clinical presentation with patches and plaques</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 90.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"120\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">C</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">(10%)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 94.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"126\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">CD4+, CD8&minus;, CD30+</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"266\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Monotonous infiltrate with cohesive sheets of large CD30+ T&nbsp;cells</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Sometimes immunoblastic/Reed&ndash;Sternberg&ndash;like cells</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Few admixed inflammatory cells</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{7104214; 10845893; 15096372}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 140.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"187\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Primary cutaneous anaplastic large cell lymphoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Clinical presentation: rapidly growing large tumour or multifocal nodules</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 6; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 140.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"187\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Mycosis fungoides, tumour stage with large cell transformation</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Clinical evolution with preceding patches and plaques; Variable expression of CD30</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 7; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 140.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"187\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; mso-ansi-language: FR;\">Adult T-cell lymphoma/leukaemia</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Detection of HTLV-1/HTLV-2, geographical clustering</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 8; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 90.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"120\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">D</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">(&lt;&nbsp;5%)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 94.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"126\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">CD4&minus;, CD8+, CD30+</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.55pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"266\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Strongly epidermotropic, sometimes pagetoid infiltrate of atypical small to medium-sized CD8+, CD30+ pleomorphic T&nbsp;cells</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">{20661014}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 140.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"187\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Primary cutaneous CD8+ aggressive epidermotropic cytotoxic T-cell lymphoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Clinical presentation: rapidly evolving erosive or ulcerated plaques and nodules; CD8+, CD30&minus; (rarely CD30+); CD45RA+ (70%)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 9; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 140.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"187\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Pagetoid reticulosis (mycosis fungoides&nbsp;subtype)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Clinical presentation: solitary erythematous and scaly lesion; various phenotypes, including expression of CD8 and CD30</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 10; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 90.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"120\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">E</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">(&lt;&nbsp;5%)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 94.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"126\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">CD4&minus;, CD8+, CD30+</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"266\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Angioinvasive infiltrates of mostly medium-sized pleomorphic CD30+ and mostly CD8+ cells</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Vascular occlusion, haemorrhage, extensive necrosis and ulceration </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{23026936}</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Note: Clinically, patients present with few papulonodular lesions that rapidly ulcerate and evolve into large, necrotic, eschar-like lesions </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{23026936}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 140.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"187\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Extranodal NK/T-cell lymphoma, nasal type</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Staging: systemic involvement; association with EBV (LMP, EBER+)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 11; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 140.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"187\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Cutaneous gamma-delta T-cell lymphoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Clinical presentation: rapidly evolving erosive or ulcerated plaques and nodules; CD56+, CD30&minus; (rarely CD30+); TCR&gamma;&delta;+ , TCR&alpha;&beta;&minus;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 12; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 140.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"187\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Primary cutaneous anaplastic large cell lymphoma (angioinvasive form)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos;\">Clinical presentation: rapidly growing large tumour with ulceration; CD4+ or CD8+, CD30+</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 13; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 90.15pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"120\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Lymphomatoid papulosis with 6p25.3 rearrangement</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">(&lt;&nbsp;5%)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 94.15pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"126\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">CD8+ or CD4/CD8 double-negative, CD30+</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 199.55pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"266\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Biphasic pattern: Epidermotropic, small to medium-sized, weakly CD30+ T&nbsp;cells with cerebriform nuclei and dense dermal infiltrate of strongly CD30+ medium-sized to large atypical cells </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">{23648461}</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Defining criterion: Chromosomal rearrangements involving the <em>DUSP22</em>-<em>IRF4</em> locus on 6p25.3</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 140.3pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"187\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Mycosis fungoides, tumour stage with large cell transformation</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Clinical evolution with preceding patches and plaques; variable expression of CD30</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">EBER, EBV-encoded small RNA.</span></p>",
